# The ledger of `image/bmp`: what Python's Pillow (its BMP plugin) lets a
# program do with BMP, one block per capability, and what Rebel answers.
# Go's standard library has no BMP (golang.org/x/image/bmp is not part of it
# and is not on this machine) and Rust's has none: `-` in their lines.
# Pillow is not installed here, so its names are those of its documented
# API, unread by `dir()`.
#
# The test files were laid out byte by byte by a Go program on 2026-11-18,
# their pixels known by construction, and every one was also read by macOS's
# `sips` into a PNG that Go's image/png decoded: equal to the byte, but for
# 16 bits of 5-5-5, where sips scales a 5-bit field otherwise than its own
# 5-6-5 (up to 7 apart); here every field is scaled the same way, rounded to
# 255.

capability bmp/decode  a BMP read: every header, depth and compression of Windows and OS/2
  heroes  image/bmp.decode, image/bmp.decode_image
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.open, BmpImagePlugin.BmpImageFile, BmpImagePlugin.DibImageFile
  note    OS/2's core header and BITMAPINFOHEADER to BITMAPV5HEADER; 1, 4, 8, 16, 24 and 32 bits; bit fields, an alpha mask making RGBA; RLE8 and RLE4; bottom up and top down. A 32-bit file with no alpha mask is RGB, its fourth byte unused as Windows documents it

capability bmp/info  the size, depth and format read from the headers
  heroes  image/bmp.info_of, image/bmp.Info
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.open (lazy)
  note    -

capability bmp/limits  a file that claims a huge image refused before it is allocated
  heroes  image/bmp.decode with image.Limits
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS
  note    -

capability bmp/encode  an image written as BMP
  heroes  image/bmp.encode
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  Image.save(format="BMP"), BmpImagePlugin._save
  note    gray as 8 bits of a gray palette and RGB as 24 bits, as Pillow writes them; RGBA as 32 bits under BITMAPV4HEADER with an alpha mask, which every reader honouring bit fields reads as alpha

capability bmp/encode-more  BMP written run-length coded, at 1 or 4 bits, or as 16 bits
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    -

capability bmp/embedded  a BMP holding a JPEG or a PNG
  heroes  refused: `unsupported`, the bytes inside are image/jpeg's and image/png's
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    -
